//--- A.axl
module A;

public fn Do()
    => Standard.Print("Do");
    
//=== stdout
Do

// Rules: _Must_ start with //@run-pass/run-panic/check
// _can_ have //@ignore-lint (errors must not be ignored)

// Modes: run-pass = Runs the program. It must run until the end. Stdout must match. Lints must be expected or ignored.
//        run-panic = Runs, it must panic. Lints must be expected or ignored.
//        check = Runs the compiler, error must be expected; lints expected or ignored

// //--- and //=== act as file splitters
// //--- FileName add a new file to the compilation
// //=== gives expected output. There must only be //=== stdout (for now)

// Lints/Errors are checked in LSP

// _Bless_ mode:
// delete //~ comments and print new ones (//~error or //~lint)
// delete everything in //=== stdout and print new

// Implementation:
// basic regex matching and file splitter
// LSP highlights only valid matches (like //@run-pass but //@blupp is not highlighted)
// LSP shows basic toy diagnostics

